1
00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:13.600
Natalie Spiska: There we go. Perfect. Alright, well, to start, if you could just briefly talk about what kind of technology your program currently uses, including any sort of wearable technology or stats website like Clip?

2
00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:18.610
Coach: So we use, for Stats, we use, Decade.

3
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:25.319
Coach: And guys have to turn their… That's in by 9 o'clock.

4
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:34.740
Coach: usually the morning after. If we're on the road at a tournament, I just… we just get it done at the end of the tournament.

5
00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:42.010
Coach: I… I actually… Dive deep into our stats. I don't really do…

6
00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:51.760
Coach: one tournament, I'm looking for trends, so I'll do… I like 6 rounds, so if I can get to 6 rounds, which we've played 6 rounds so far.

7
00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:53.420
Coach: So, I like to look at…

8
00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:59.620
Coach: tournament rounds, not practice. I don't really have a… unless it's qualifying, we don't track that.

9
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.699
Coach: If they're just playing, like, 9 holes and trying to hit situational shots, we don't track any of that.

10
00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:11.819
Coach: We have a Zen putting green upstairs, which is a green that moves, it's pretty cool.

11
00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:12.350
Natalie Spiska: Yeah.

12
00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:14.090
Coach: We get a lot of use out of that.

13
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.710
Coach: Some of the guys are aim-pointers, like me, and…

14
00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:22.499
Coach: They'll set it to be able to calibrate themselves a little bit better.

15
00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:30.949
Coach: We have a Quintech, we use it lightly. We have a sand putt lab that we use a lot.

16
00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.489
Coach: We have two quads, that we use a ton of, and then we use… we have,

17
00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:45.699
Coach: two track bands, and apparently Trackman plural is track bands, which I didn't… I didn't know that.

18
00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.940
Natalie Spiska: Weird, truckmen.

19
00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:55.030
Coach: I thought it was gonna be TrackMen, but it's TrackMen. We do a ton… we do a ton of combines. We have a weekly

20
00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:58.070
Coach: combine requirement. We have a…

21
00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:03.449
Coach: One that we set up from 50 yards to 150 yards that they have to have a certain score on.

22
00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:07.069
Coach: And we'll… we'll keep a leaderboard of that.

23
00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:12.390
Coach: Other than that, I, I like…

24
00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:21.170
Coach: Using the technology indoors, obviously, since this semester has been pretty white, and we haven't been able to get outside much.

25
00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:25.359
Coach: It's been very productive to track numbers and

26
00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.420
Coach: To, work on some wedge…

27
00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:33.749
Coach: watch distances, so that's been productive. But other than that.

28
00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:39.310
Coach: Yeah, we don't have anything… anything else other than that. It's a nice collection, we're very blessed.

29
00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:51.679
Natalie Spiska: Yeah, I was gonna say, that's… that's a lot of technology that you guys have, especially Decade. I've used it in the past, but, like, very briefly. But, like, how has… how has Decade been implemented into your guys', like, training program?

30
00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:59.010
Coach: Sure, so we have our guys go on track, man, and they set up

31
00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:04.299
Coach: On… we have one account for each guy, and we have them track

32
00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:09.580
Coach: There's shot dispersion ellipses, so that we can discuss with them

33
00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:13.510
Coach: What shots to hit under certain conditions.

34
00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.830
Coach: Especially on par 3s,

35
00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:26.179
Coach: you know, when I coached on the women's side, we didn't see too many 220, 240-yard par 3s. We're seeing quite a few of them now.

36
00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:31.839
Coach: Yeah. On the men's side. So, I think it's important to understand

37
00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:39.069
Coach: What a player's tendencies are, and you know, the nice thing is we can…

38
00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:43.500
Coach: Really take some deep dives, and after a tournament.

39
00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:46.839
Coach: Where all their stats are in,

40
00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:51.430
Coach: Decade actually has, like, a shot tracker, like a… like a shot link.

41
00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:55.850
Coach: That the guys put in, and I can track how we play

42
00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:59.449
Coach: Or what it looks like, or how we played each hole.

43
00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:00.870
Coach: Which is really.

44
00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:01.670
Natalie Spiska: Interesting.

45
00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:02.340
Natalie Spiska: Yeah.

46
00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:03.420
Coach: Yeah, so…

47
00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:10.869
Coach: you know, if a guy's like, oh man, I was standing in the middle of the fairway to make double bogey, well, like, how'd you make double bogey? And then you can actually go in and see that

48
00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:14.189
Coach: They hit it in the bunker, hit it over the green.

49
00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.770
Coach: Chipped it to 20 feet, and then 2-putt.

50
00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:17.970
Natalie Spiska: Yeah.

51
00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:25.800
Coach: I think it's a great thing to use, because I think college golfers talk 68, shoot 78, and act 88, so…

52
00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:26.570
Natalie Spiska: Yeah.

53
00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:38.330
Coach: it's one of those things where we think… and it's a human thing, I think. We think we're way better than we are, so I think it brings you down into a realistic world when you're like, oh yeah, I, you know, I…

54
00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:45.610
Coach: I played number 420. Alright, well, why did you do that? Well, I drove into the bunker twice.

55
00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:51.979
Coach: and then I got it underneath that lip. Well, maybe you shouldn't have hit driver there, right? And…

56
00:04:52.600 --> 00:05:00.690
Coach: it does a lot with course management. Obviously, the videos are fantastic. And full disclosure, I'm a good, close, personal friend of

57
00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:02.670
Coach: Scott Fawcett.

58
00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:04.080
Natalie Spiska: Oh, nice!

59
00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:08.069
Coach: I was one… I… yeah, I went to one of his first,

60
00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:12.510
Coach: lectures that he did at Baltistrrol back in…

61
00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:21.399
Coach: like, 2014 or 15, and I was just enamored with it. I went away from it for a little bit.

62
00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:26.389
Coach: But I think the educational component in Decade is really, really good.

63
00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:33.260
Coach: You know, some of the drills, and then obviously the talking about how to practice, shot dispersion.

64
00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:37.799
Coach: Because I'm sure [Author's Coach] could tell you the same thing. I'm gonna tell you here, that…

65
00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:45.720
Coach: Even if we say it, if Scott Fawcett says it, it's completely different, it's so much more powerful, so…

66
00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:46.339
Natalie Spiska: Likely, yeah.

67
00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:52.479
Coach: I like to have as many, yeah, I like to have as many, arrows in my quiver as possible, so…

68
00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.570
Coach: We do a lot with that decade.

69
00:05:55.240 --> 00:06:01.140
Natalie Spiska: Yeah, that sounds good. How's the use of technology in your program changed over, like, the last few years?

70
00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:06.389
Coach: Yeah, we used to have to beg guys to put stats in, and it was.

71
00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:06.740
Natalie Spiska: Yeah.

72
00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:11.759
Coach: hard, but as our team has gotten more and more competitive over the years.

73
00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:13.709
Coach: It's really not so much of a thing.

74
00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:19.910
Coach: Trackman and the quads have been…

75
00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:24.789
Coach: Like, I don't think we hit a ball upstairs without a launch monitor on it.

76
00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:31.840
Coach: It's very rare that we hit a ball upstairs, unless somebody's working on a feel, or they're working on a swing lesson.

77
00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:35.809
Coach: something they're doing with their Home Pro.

78
00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:41.570
Coach: Just because, you know, when we're upstairs and we don't have ball flight, you want to see what the ball's doing.

79
00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:48.079
Coach: Because obviously that's the most important thing, because you want the golf ball to be your coach, and I talk about that a lot.

80
00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:53.349
Coach: But, you know, I think a lot more guys are using

81
00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:59.349
Coach: The launch monitors, with a… we just hired an assistant coach.

82
00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:10.170
Coach: And he's become really proficient in the sand putt lab, so our guys hop on that at least once a week. That's been really good. That's like a track man for putting, so it's been very productive.

83
00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:19.350
Natalie Spiska: Yeah, I was gonna say, we had a sand putt lab, and we only used it briefly, because it was loaned to us by one of our… my teammates' coaches, but how do you.

84
00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:19.669
Coach: Huh.

85
00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:25.649
Natalie Spiska: the Samputt Lab as, like, that track man? Like, are you just checking to make sure your stroke's online, or…

86
00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:26.750
Natalie Spiska: How's it?

87
00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:31.609
Coach: Yeah, I mean, I think sometimes you can give athletes too much information.

88
00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:39.910
Coach: So, the great thing about [Assistant Coach] is he doesn't let them take too deep of a dive and try to break down their putting stroke too much.

89
00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:41.090
Coach: Yeah.

90
00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:49.659
Coach: It has a feedback system in the most recent update, where it'll tell you what the clubface is doing, if it's open or closed at impact.

91
00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:54.289
Coach: which is something I harp on. We want to make sure we're returning the club as…

92
00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:58.049
Coach: As close to square or zero as possible.

93
00:07:58.330 --> 00:07:59.310
Natalie Spiska: Yeah.

94
00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:06.209
Coach: But I think technology, especially with your generation, because you guys are so smart with technology that it… it could be…

95
00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:14.049
Coach: It could be, detrimental as well. When we first got TrackMan.

96
00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:19.889
Coach: We had two guys that were upstairs all the time.

97
00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:25.599
Coach: And [Player 1], who, was one of the best players to ever play at [University].

98
00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:31.980
Coach: [Player 1] played, would hit balls in the thing and wouldn't really care. Just wanted to know how far is the ball going?

99
00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:35.810
Coach: And then, how far, you know, how much thin he had on the golf ball.

100
00:08:36.679 --> 00:08:46.270
Coach: And then, his best friend growing up, [Player 2], unfortunately, he didn't realize how much all of the information would bother him.

101
00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:53.710
Natalie Spiska: So we go to our first tournament, and he's just freaking out. He's like, I can't believe I got so many things going on in my mind.

102
00:08:54.080 --> 00:09:00.300
Coach: So, when we got back, he and I were hitting balls upstairs, and I just turned all the tiles off.

103
00:09:00.590 --> 00:09:04.449
Coach: And just left on, you know, carry number.

104
00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:09.059
Coach: And club head speed, because he wanted to see how far… how hard he was hitting it.

105
00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:17.680
Coach: that was… that was massive for [Player 2]. He was a great player. I mean, he was a [University] Player of the Year, and that was massive for him, because he needed…

106
00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:19.679
Coach: To be able to just see how far he hit it.

107
00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:25.420
Coach: And then you have some kids you probably have on your team that need to know everything. Angle of attack.

108
00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:32.370
Coach: You know, you know, our, backspin, sidespin…

109
00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:35.819
Coach: Low point, that's become a new hot one.

110
00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:36.710
Natalie Spiska: Yeah.

111
00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:41.030
Coach: You know, it's… it's… you gotta be careful how you use the technology, for sure.

112
00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:47.789
Coach: And the other thing is, I don't really want to be a guy who leans on technology when you're trying to coach golfers to score.

113
00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:53.270
Coach: Because… the search for perfect, and I'll say this a thousand times to our guys.

114
00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:57.709
Coach: The search for perfect really ruins a lot of golfers.

115
00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:00.439
Coach: Especially young ones, because…

116
00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:08.510
Coach: You know, you know kids that once you hand them a scorecard, they play… they play completely different.

117
00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:11.099
Coach: And when they're on the range, they look lost.

118
00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:16.279
Coach: But if you get them out in a match against somebody, it's… it's something pretty nice.

119
00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:22.190
Coach: But then again, you get some kids who really need to know techno… need to know their numbers.

120
00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:25.270
Coach: Their launch conditions and all that other garbage, but…

121
00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:30.029
Coach: I'm not chasing or coaching golf swings, I'm chasing guys that could put a scorecard together.

122
00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:45.309
Natalie Spiska: Yeah, I definitely agree with that. Also, being, like… I wouldn't say I'm too reliant on technology, but I definitely do like to know what my numbers are around a certain area, so, yeah. So what do you do… what do you do if…

123
00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:46.860
Coach: If your numbers are off.

124
00:10:47.520 --> 00:11:06.569
Natalie Spiska: If my numbers are off, this happened to me last season. Honestly, I didn't look at or video my swing for, like, the entirety of last spring semester. I knew what was happening, I was just like, as long as I'm, like, hitting it where I need to go, it doesn't need to be pretty. So for me, I have to completely shut it off. I'm not looking at anything.

125
00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:22.029
Natalie Spiska: It's gotten a lot better now, so a big thing for me is club path, because I have a tendency to just go a little bit over the top, and I really, really don't like it. So, if my club path is positive, I like that. If it's negative, it bothers me, but…

126
00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:24.850
Natalie Spiska: I've gotten better at with it through the years.

127
00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:28.699
Coach: That's good. That's good. Well, at least you can… at least you can self…

128
00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:34.979
Coach: analyze and then fix that on your own. There's a lot of people who can't. They need that technology.

129
00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:38.370
Natalie Spiska: It's taken me a while to get to this point, though, I will admit, so…

130
00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:43.540
Coach: Sure, golf isn't easy, it's hard. Ball's on the ground, you gotta get it off the ground, it's not easy.

131
00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:50.489
Natalie Spiska: Yeah, exactly. Are there any particular skill areas that you think technology has the biggest impact?

132
00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:53.860
Natalie Spiska: Like, ball striking, in your putting, short game.

133
00:11:54.670 --> 00:12:03.569
Coach: I think centerness of strike with a putter, so making sure that the sand putt lab is calibrated correctly, flat, and level.

134
00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:08.349
Coach: I think that's massive, because the center of the strike

135
00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:24.449
Coach: for a putt is so massively important, and they see guys on TV with a bad camera angle, and they're like, oh, well, this guy's not center… this guy's not hitting it on the center. Well, he may not be setting up on the center, but he's most certainly striking it on the center. If you go back and you look at it.

136
00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:27.160
Coach: I think that the really good stuff

137
00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:33.889
Coach: that Trackman is moving towards. They have an AI version now, have you seen Tracy?

138
00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:41.109
Natalie Spiska: Tracy, yeah, I've seen… I haven't used it, but one of my teammates was using it, and she's like, Tracy hates my swing. I go, okay.

139
00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:45.070
Coach: So I… I…

140
00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:51.390
Coach: I hop on there, and I taught for a living, back in the day, and

141
00:12:52.240 --> 00:13:06.459
Coach: I think it's genius what they're doing, is they're taking the information and they're telling you what to work on. And then they give you three options, right? Like, they give you three… like, for me, it's dynamic loft, because my pelvis stalls and I get a little flippy.

142
00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:17.540
Coach: So, I work on that, and there's… the great thing is, talking to the track band folks, I'm like, how close are you guys away from wiping out

143
00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:19.969
Coach: like, human instructors.

144
00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:24.299
Coach: And they've made a commitment internally that they just won't do that.

145
00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:39.720
Coach: So, obviously, Tracy doesn't tell you what to work on, like, oh, you need to get the handle more forward. It just… it just gives you numbers of, alright, your dynamic loft for a 7-iron is, I don't know, like, 30… 36 or something like that.

146
00:13:39.970 --> 00:13:41.359
Coach: And,

147
00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:48.099
Coach: you know, it'll tell you, give you a feedback of where it needs to be. I think that's… that's really great.

148
00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:52.090
Coach: And what you could probably use, Tracy, with is your path.

149
00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:55.590
Coach: And telling you where your path is, and giving you feedback.

150
00:13:55.750 --> 00:13:58.309
Coach: But other than that, I think,

151
00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:07.629
Coach: The impact part of Trackband is massive. I think that's really big, like, when you can go in to go impact location.

152
00:14:08.010 --> 00:14:12.189
Coach: I think that's really important, but… I love the fact that

153
00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:21.690
Coach: you can get proper distance numbers indoors with a quad and a trackman now. Trackman, when it first came out, wasn't very good indoors.

154
00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:23.110
Natalie Spiska: Yeah.

155
00:14:23.110 --> 00:14:27.310
Coach: From… yeah, because we don't have a lot of ball flight where we're at upstairs in Gample.

156
00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:38.079
Coach: So the quad has been fantastic. The guys love it, too. You can do competitions on it, and combine type of events on the quad as well.

157
00:14:40.180 --> 00:14:51.359
Natalie Spiska: Has the putting green that you also mentioned, has that helped in any way of being able to use those certain greens and slopes? Because we have something similar, it just, like, adjusts, but it's… it's not that good for, like.

158
00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:53.240
Natalie Spiska: You know, long distance, obviously.

159
00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:54.650
Coach: You want to plug you?

160
00:14:54.900 --> 00:15:01.079
Natalie Spiska: I believe it is a putt view, it's just a flat surface that moves up and down for, different angles, so…

161
00:15:01.390 --> 00:15:04.680
Natalie Spiska: So ours is a Zen putting green.

162
00:15:04.910 --> 00:15:05.560
Natalie Spiska: Okay.

163
00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:07.860
Coach: It's from England.

164
00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:12.570
Coach: We have 1, 2… we have 5 holes on it.

165
00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:15.610
Coach: And all four corners…

166
00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:20.109
Coach: It, like, starts like this, but you can turn it… you can actually bend it, like.

167
00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:23.700
Coach: Like a foam noodle. You can bend it like a foam noodle.

168
00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:25.369
Natalie Spiska: Interesting.

169
00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:37.529
Coach: Yeah, it's… it's really good. I think, I want to get the new turf that they have, it's like lamb wool or something, to where it's a lot more smoother. We have a synthetic turf top right now.

170
00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:42.209
Coach: Yeah, I mean, it's… it's… it's been good for breaking putts.

171
00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:49.300
Coach: You know, and we don't… we don't go crazy. I mean, I set it up to do uphill putts if I have guys that aren't getting it.

172
00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:52.569
Coach: To the hole, or having a hard time getting it to the hole.

173
00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:58.369
Coach: But, like, I say all this… not only to say that

174
00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:01.980
Coach: Like, I just love a good old-fashioned golf ball, or a…

175
00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:04.789
Coach: Or, you know, like a putting string.

176
00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:09.610
Coach: Yeah. You know, I… I like…

177
00:16:09.910 --> 00:16:14.350
Coach: Putt-out has a new thing that I pull out at golf camps all the time.

178
00:16:14.690 --> 00:16:18.650
Coach: It's their wacky ball, it's got a flat side and a round side.

179
00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:22.050
Coach: I think that's really great, because,

180
00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:26.380
